        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-white">The Bowflex Treadmill 10 is discontinued, and a used one is worth buying
            only if it is cheap and you want decline or a 400 lb rating.</strong> Its checked figures are strong:
            a 22 by 60-inch deck, -5% to 15%, 12 mph and a 10-inch touchscreen. But its warranty did not transfer
            to a second owner, Bowflex never published its motor rating, and its console has to be registered to
            your own JRNY account.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Everyone else should buy new: the
            <a href="/bowflex-t9-treadmill/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">Bowflex T9</a>
            for the same deck with a lifetime frame and motor warranty, or the T16 if a built-in screen is what
            will keep you training.
          </p>
